    "number": 59,
    "id": "113-Q059",
    "answer": "C",
    "explanation": "有關Poly (ADP-ribose) polymerase (PARP) inhibitor治療相關敘述及臨床試驗，下列敘述何者**錯誤**？ \n(A) Phase III OlympiA trial 證實 adjuvant olaparib 在high risk gBRCA mutation (TNBC or Luminal BC手術後) 有EFS及OS befefit. \n(B) Four different PARP inhibitors (olaparib, rucaparib, niraparib, and talazoparib) have now received regulatory approval in the United States for the treatment of ovarian cancer, breast, prostate, and pancreatic cancers with BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutations and in some cases other defects in DNA repair by homologous recombination. \n(C) The FDA has approved rucaparib and olaparib for men with metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer (mCRPC) who have certain genetic mutations based on the EMBRACA trials. \n(D) PARP 抑制 IC50: olaparib > rucaparib > talazoparib.    \n(E) in NOVA trial, niraparib has demonstrated survival benefit in platinum-sensitive, recurrent ovarian cancer, regardless of the presence or absence of gBRCA mutations or homologous recombination deficiency (HRD) status. \n\n解答: C\n\n詳解:\n\n(A) [Image 1]\nTNBC or Luminal BC手術後, adjuvant olaparib 3y DFS 為 85.9 vs. 77.1%, HR 0.58, p<0.001; OS 為 92.0% vs. 88.3%, HR 0.68, p=0.02\n\n(B)\nolaparib was approved for ovarian, breast, pancreatic and prostate cancer\nrucaparib was approved for ovarian and prostate cancer\nniraparib was approved for ovarian cancer\ntalazoparib was approved for breast and prostate cancer\n\n(C) EMBRACA trial 研究對象為 Talazoparib in Patients with Advanced Breast Cancer and a Germline BRCA Mutation\n\n(D)\nOlaparib IC 50 = 68.5 uM\nrucaparib IC 50 = 53.7 uM\nTalazoparib IC 50 =  8.40 uM\n\n(E) [Image 2]\ngBRCA cohort, mPFS 21.0m vs. 5.5m, HR 0.27, p<0.001\nnon-gBRCA cohort, mPFS 9.3m vs. 3.9m, HR 0.45, p<0.001\n\n\n參考:\nAdjuvant Olaparib for Patients with BRCA1- or BRCA2-Mutated Breast Cancer\nhttps://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMoa2105215\n\nFDA aprroved for olaparib, rucaparib, niraparib, and talazoparib\nhttps://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2020/208558s014lbl.pdf\nhttps://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/209115s011lbl.pdf\nhttps://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2020/208447s015s017lbledt.pdf\nhttps://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/217439s000lbl.pdf\n\nTalazoparib in Patients with Advanced Breast Cancer and a Germline BRCA Mutation\nhttps://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMoa1802905\n\nolaparib, rucaparib, talazoparib IC50\nhttps://www.cancerrxgene.org/compound/Olaparib/1017/overview/ic50\nhttps://www.cancerrxgene.org/compound/Rucaparib/1175/overview/ic50\nhttps://www.cancerrxgene.org/compound/Talazoparib/1259/overview/ic50?screening_set=GDSC1\n\nNiraparib Maintenance Therapy in Platinum-Sensitive, Recurrent Ovarian Cancer\nhttps://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMoa1611310",
    "questionTextFromExplanationFile": "有關Poly (ADP-ribose) polymerase (PARP) inhibitor治療相關敘述及臨床試驗，下列敘述何者**錯誤**？",
