    "explanation": "(1)正確\nMAPS trial: randomized, controlled, open-label, Phase 3 trial. (Lancet 2016;387:1405-1414)\n\nBackground: assess the effect on survival of bevacizumab when added to the present standard of care, cisplatin plus pemetrexed, as first-line treatment of advanced malignant pleural mesothelioma\n\nKey inclusion criteria: unresectable malignant pleural mesothelioma, chemotherapy naive, ECOG 0–2, no substantial cardiovascular comorbidity, not amenable to curative surgery\n\nRegimen:\nPCB Q3W (up to 6cycles): pemetrexed (500 mg/m2) + cisplatin (75 mg/m2) + bevacizumab (15mg/kg)\nPC Q3W (up to 6cycles): pemetrexed (500 mg/m2) + cisplatin (75 mg/m2) \n\nFindings\nMedian OS: PCB vs.PC\n           18.8 vs. 16.1 months\n           (HR: 0.77, p-value: 0.0167)\n\n\n(2)正確\nUseful IHC markers include: \n- positive markers to confirm mesothelial differentiation, such as WT1, calretinin, and D2-40\n- negative markers to exclude mimics, such as polyclonal carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA), thyroid transcription factor-1 (TTF-1), and claudin-4.\n- One of the caveats is that no individual IHC marker is entirely sensitive and specific.\n- Therefore, it is recommended that a panel including at least two mesothelial markers (eg, calretinin, WT1, D2-40) and two carcinoma markers (eg, claudin-4, TTF-1, polyclonal CEA) should be used to establish the diagnosis.\n\nNCCN guideline v2.2025 – Principles of pathologic review (Page 11/61) \n\n(3)正確。 epithelioid & non-epithelioid 皆有OS benefit，但non-epithelioid組HR較低且forest plot沒跨過中線 (見explain_figure 1)\n(4)錯誤。此trial 為 Nivo + Ipi vs. chemo\n\nCheckmate-743 trial: a multicenter, randomized, open-label, phase 3\nLancet 2021;397:375-386\nAnnals of Oncology2022, Volume 33, Issue 5, 488 - 499\n\nBackground: \n– Approved systemic treatments for malignant pleural mesothelioma (MPM) have been limited to chemotherapy (moderate survival benefit with poor outcomes). \n– Nivolumab plus ipilimumab has shown clinical benefit in other tumour types, including 1L NSCLC \n– Hypothesis: Nivo + Ipi would improve overall survival in MPM.\n\nKey inclusion criteria: previously untreated, histologically confirmed, unresectable MPM and ECOG ≤1\n\nExperimental arm: Nivolumab (3 mg/kg)Q2W + Ipilimumab (1 mg/kg) Q6W for up to 2 years\nControl arm: platinum plus pemetrexed chemotherapy, 6 cycles\n\nFindings: \nNivolumab + ipilimumab to prolong OS versus chemotherapy across subgroups, including histology. Median OS of \n– All patients: 18.1 vs. 14.1 mo, HR 0.73\n– Epithelioid: 18.2 vs. 16.7 mo, HR 0.85\n– Non epithelioid: 18.1 vs. 8.8 mo, HR 0.48\n\n<補充：比較MAPS和CM-743>\n值得注意的是MAPS以及CM-743都有排除CNS metastasis\nMAPS中epithelioid以及non-epithelioid似乎都偏向使用cis+alimta+beva，但都沒有達到統計上的顯著差異(Epitheloid HR:0.82(0.64-1.06);non-epitheloid HR:0.64(0.40-1.02))\n而在CM-743中的subgroup analysis, PD-L1>=1%相較於<1%對於使用nivo+ipi在median OS的好處更大(>=1%, HR:0.69(0.55-0.87);<1%, HR:0.94(0.62-1.40))",
    "questionTextFromExplanationFile": "下列關於 Malignant pleural mesothelioma 的敘述中,正確的有?\n(1) 根據 phase 3 randomized trial (MAPS),在 unresectable malignant pleural mesotheliom病人,bevacizumab 加上 chemotherapy 相較於 chemotherapy alone 可顯著延長 overall survival。\n(2) 病理上,malignant pleural mesothelioma 常呈現 positive 的 immunohistochemical marker 為 WT1, calretinin, and D2-40; thyroid transcription factor-1 (TTF-1)常為 negative\n(3) 根據 CheckMate 743 trial,immune checkpoint inhibitors 的 overall survival benefit 主要發生在非上皮型(Non-epithelioid)的病人族群。\n(4) CheckMate 743 trial 顯示,在 unresectable malignant pleural mesothelioma 病人,nivolumab + chemotherapy 相較於 chemotherapy 可顯著延長 overall survival (OS)",
