    "explanation": "Breast cancer-related lymphedema (BCRL)\n(1)錯誤；根據文獻內提及，過往研究axillary lymph node dissection (ALND) 比起sentinel lymph node biopsy (SLNB)，發生BCRL的比率是19.9% (95% CI: 13.5–28.2)及 5.6%，比率約為4倍，非10倍\n(2)錯誤；根據文獻內提及，過往研究發現與治療無關的BCRL risk factors 為obesity、subclinical edema及cellulitis，所以瘦的病人發生機會比較低\n(3)錯誤；文獻內提到，\"there is no limitation on the maximum amount of weight that can be lifted as long as weight-lifting exercises are supervised and progressive\"，舉重物及其最大重量並沒有被限制，間接表示與BCRL無關。\n(4)正確；National cancer institute 在lymphedema頁面，有提到\"it is a chronic condition that cannot be cured but can be treated to relieve swelling and improve your ability to function day to day\"；另根據Johns Hopkins Medicine 網站內\"Breast cancer lymphedema after treatment\"文章，提到\"It’s a chronic (ongoing) condition that has no cure\"\n\n\nRef: \n1.Gillespie TC, Sayegh HE, Brunelle CL, Daniell KM, Taghian AG. Breast cancer-related lymphedema: risk factors, precautionary measures, and treatments. Gland Surg. 2018 Aug;7(4):379-403. doi: 10.21037/gs.2017.11.04.\n2.https://www.hopkinsmedicine.org/health/conditions-and-diseases/breast-cancer/breast-cancer-lymphedema-after-treatment\n3.https://www.cancer.gov/about-cancer/treatment/side-effects/lymphedema",
